# Local Worker secrets for `wrangler dev` / `opennextjs-cloudflare preview`.
# Copy to .dev.vars (git-ignored); never commit a value.
#
# The service-role key: server code only (the Stripe webhook's sync, the
# customer mapping, /api/health). In stage and prod every deploy sets it as a
# Worker secret from the Supabase root's wiring document; here it is yours.
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=
#
# Stripe. Unset, the pricing page shows the template's sample plans with
# checkout off, checkout and the portal answer "Stripe is not connected." and
# the webhook answers 503. In stage and prod these are Worker secrets the
# owner sets once per environment:
# `wrangler secret put <NAME> --name subscription-payments-web-<env>`
# (README, "Connect Stripe").
# STRIPE_SECRET_KEY=sk_test_***
# STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET=whsec_***
# STRIPE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=pk_test_***
#
# The Supabase URL and anon key, and the site's origin, are wrangler vars
# (rendered into wrangler.jsonc, which the build inlines); put real values
# here only to point a local Worker at a real project's server side.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=
